# Atomic Design Structure

## Component Organization

Follow strict atomic design hierarchy:

### Atoms (`src/components/atoms/`)
- Basic building blocks (Button, Logo, Input, etc.)
- Single responsibility components
- No dependencies on other components except utilities
- Examples: [Logo.tsx](mdc:src/components/atoms/Logo.tsx), [Button.tsx](mdc:src/components/atoms/Button.tsx), [CTAButton.tsx](mdc:src/components/atoms/CTAButton.tsx)

### Molecules (`src/components/molecules/`)
- Combinations of atoms
- Reusable UI patterns
- Examples: [NavigationMenu.tsx](mdc:src/components/molecules/NavigationMenu.tsx), [HeaderActions.tsx](mdc:src/components/molecules/HeaderActions.tsx)

### Organisms (`src/components/organisms/`)
- Complex components combining molecules and atoms
- Complete sections of UI
- Examples: [HeroSection.tsx](mdc:src/components/organisms/HeroSection.tsx)

### Templates (`src/components/templates/`)
- Page-level components
- Layout definitions

## Rules

1. **Atoms** must not import other atoms/molecules/organisms
2. **Molecules** can import atoms but not other molecules/organisms
3. **Organisms** can import atoms and molecules
4. **Templates** can import any component type
5. Always use TypeScript interfaces for props
6. Export default the main component
7. Use descriptive component names that reflect their purpose
